{
  "title": "Independently check and use the f68r1 map of 29 star-label loci",
  "statement": "This is the f68r1 panel component of P-L4-031. It supplies approximate native Yale first-glyph positions for all 29 ZL star-label loci f68r1.8 through f68r1.36. Voynichese word boxes were registered to the left panel of the unfolded Yale recto. Inside the star field, Takahashi's readings match the 29 boxes one-to-one. Six ZL readings differ from Takahashi. For the duplicate otor, the other companion occurrence lies in the upper paragraph. Each first-glyph point was examined on the native crop, with a second reading of the six variant matches and the duplicate. A contributor who did not annotate f68r1 can verify the locations before joining them to the independent blind pictures. The coordinates themselves express location and carry no proposed reading in a target language.",
  "program": "L4",
  "check": "Check coverage of all 29 ZL Ls IDs and unique word-box assignments. Have a separate contributor recover at least three frozen loci f68r1.12, f68r1.26 and f68r1.30 on the linked native crop without the recorded positions, then compare the selected word and first-glyph point. Review f68r1.32 before any join that assumes labels always lie to the right. Use only agreed blind picture features for cross-panel tests.",
